{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019mmMyNJLuLUyTBv95Kkvjt","type":"tool_result","content":"515\t\n516\tA ticket passes when a round ends with no open findings and\n517\tat least `minRounds` rounds have run. With `minRounds: 2`, a\n518\tclean first round is followed by a second review before the\n519\tticket merges. When the review in round `maxRounds` leaves\n520\tfindings open, the ticket becomes `ready-for-human` (unresolved)\n521\twith its branch kept, and the fixer does not run after that\n522\tfinal review. A reviewer that exits non-zero, times out or writes\n523\tfindings redeye cannot parse fails the attempt.\n524\t\n525\tEvery round is appended to\n526\t`.scratch/<feature>/reviews/<ticket file name>`: the findings and\n527\ttheir verdicts, the fixer's response to each (fixed, or disputed\n528\twith its reason), the test result and the branch head after the\n529\tfix.\n530\t\n531\tA missing file or a file with no `adversarial` key leaves\n532\tbehavior unchanged. Invalid JSON, an `adversarial` value that\n533\tis not an object, a missing role, or an invalid role string\n534\tstops the run before any branch or worktree is created\n535\t(exit 2).\n536\t\n537\tWith `adversarial` set, a bare `redeye` runs tickets with the\n538\t`implement` role. A provider on the command line replaces the\n539\twhole `implement` role for that run (its flags do not carry\n540\tover), and redeye logs one line saying so. Flags inside a role\n541\tstring win for that role; run-wide flags such as `-m` or\n542\t`--effort` fill in whatever the string leaves out, for both\n543\troles:\n544\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37a0e722-681e-439b-ad4f-0778a23ce452","uuid":"38822f74-5d50-4a74-887c-6d51a7d69b99","timestamp":"2026-11-21T03:35:27.283Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/redeye.adversarial-review-06-resume-an-interrupted-loop/README.md","content":"\nA ticket passes when a round ends with no open findings and\nat least `minRounds` rounds have run. With `minRounds: 2`, a\nclean first round is followed by a second review before the\nticket merges. When the review in round `maxRounds` leaves\nfindings open, the ticket becomes `ready-for-human` (unresolved)\nwith its branch kept, and the fixer does not run after that\nfinal review. A reviewer that exits non-zero, times out or writes\nfindings redeye cannot parse fails the attempt.\n\nEvery round is appended to\n`.scratch/<feature>/reviews/<ticket file name>`: the findings and\ntheir verdicts, the fixer's response to each (fixed, or disputed\nwith its reason), the test result and the branch head after the\nfix.\n\nA missing file or a file with no `adversarial` key leaves\nbehavior unchanged. Invalid JSON, an `adversarial` value that\nis not an object, a missing role, or an invalid role string\nstops the run before any branch or worktree is created\n(exit 2).\n\nWith `adversarial` set, a bare `redeye` runs tickets with the\n`implement` role. A provider on the command line replaces the\nwhole `implement` role for that run (its flags do not carry\nover), and redeye logs one line saying so. Flags inside a role\nstring win for that role; run-wide flags such as `-m` or\n`--effort` fill in whatever the string leaves out, for both\nroles:\n","numLines":30,"startLine":515,"totalLines":920}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019mmMyNJLuLUyTBv95Kkvjt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFNZnSgA47kEnGuGPKqt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012NJnpPmkAAhQTCogG4qkGG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"with its reason), the test result and the branch head after the\nfix.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"with its reason), the test result and the branch head after the\nfix. Each entry is committed as it is written.\n\nIf a run is interrupted mid-loop, the next run resumes the ticket\nat the round after the last one recorded, without implementing it\nagain. This happens only when the ticket branch still exists, its\nhead matches the head the log last recorded, and the log has no\npass, unresolved or failed entry after that round. Otherwise the\nstale branch is removed and the ticket starts fresh.\n\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='AGENTS.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"  follows the same sentinel and append-only conventions as the\n  other logs.\n\"\"\",\"\"\"  follows the same sentinel and append-only conventions as the\n  other logs. Each entry is committed as it is appended, not only\n  at terminal points: resume reads the log from the base checkout,\n  and an uncommitted log would trip the dirty-tree check on the\n  next run, so the interrupted loop could never resume.\n- Fresh and resumed attempts share one round loop,\n  `runAdversarialLoop` in `src/orchestrator.ts`; a resume only\n  changes its start round. Keep round logic there.\n\"\"\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"- tapzero's `t.throws` is async\"\"\",\"\"\"- The fake pi's `FAKE_PI_RESPONSES` takes `hang` (never exits),\n  for interrupting a CLI run mid-loop: wait until\n  `FAKE_PI_COUNTER` shows the hanging call started, then SIGINT\n- tapzero's `t.throws` is async\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat; npm run lint 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence